       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5\u201310 mg. 50 mg is five times the maximum and could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and prolonged toxicity. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. I can't confirm that this order was clinically intended.\n\nThe prescriber should confirm the intended dose. If they meant 5 mg or 10 mg once daily by mouth, I can enter it once they or you confirm that. Orders for patients on the medicine service should be placed or co-signed by the treating clinician."
