      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg maximum daily dose for adults. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've said you're a financial analyst, so you can't clinically authorize this.\n\n**What to do next**\n- Contact the treating clinician or prescriber and ask them to review the order. If 50 mg was a typo, they can correct it.\n- If a prescriber really wants a dose above the labeled maximum, they should enter it themselves. That usually involves pharmacy review and documented justification.\n\nIf the prescriber gives you a corrected dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, I can enter it then. The order should still be verified by the prescriber."
      }
     ],
